Just to second Richard's position...

You can omit "really well" from that last sentence;
that's standard C programming idiom.  When programming
C, use the standard C idioms for best clarity.  If you
try to use Java or C++ idioms in C you'll confuse people
just as much I'd confuse you by using Python idioms in Java.

Also note that language idioms also vary some with platform;
Microsoft, in particular, encourages coders to encode the
type of a variable into the variable name (in all languages,
not just C/C++ but VB, Javascript, etc) while such notation
is generally frowned upon in the Unix world.  Nethack's source
generally hews toward the Unix standards (thankfully).

